+   **Tracker duplicates.** Before a candidate goes into any tracker Issue (this session's `retro-candidates` Issue in collect mode, or an Issue of its own), first search the open Issues, open `retro` and `retro-candidates` Issues included, for every file, script, and skill name the candidate mentions; on GitHub: `gh issue list --state open --search "<name> in:title,body" --json number,title`. An open Issue on the same problem gets a comment with this session's evidence instead, and the candidate stays out of the new Issue. One that only shares the file for a different problem becomes the blocker of a new `retro` Issue (`blocked_by`; on GitHub `gh issue edit <new> --add-blocked-by <existing>`), so the two never edit that file in parallel; a `retro-candidates` Issue gets no `blocked_by`, which would hold the whole collection behind it: `/retro-collect` checks shared files when it implements.
